-- ============================================================
-- Warrior (Protection): Intervene becomes an enemy charge
-- ============================================================
-- Redesign of woa_2026_08_09_05.sql / _18.sql.  Intervene is now Protection's
-- Charge: you leap at an ENEMY, not at a party member.
--
-- Why the whole ability changes rather than just the target.  Charge is Battle
-- Stance only and Intercept is Berserker Stance only, so the one spec that is
-- required to stand in Defensive Stance had no gap closer at all -- a
-- Protection warrior who lost a target simply walked.  Intervene was the
-- obvious donor: it is already a SPELL_EFFECT_CHARGE, already Defensive Stance
-- only (Stances 131072), already on a 30 second cooldown, and its actual job --
-- soaking one attack aimed at somebody else -- is worth nothing on a solo fork.
--
-- Three things had to move, and the second and third are the ones that would
-- have silently misbehaved if only the target type were flipped:
--
-- 1. EffectImplicitTargetA on effects 1 and 3: 57 (TARGET_UNIT_TARGET_RAID) ->
--    6 (TARGET_UNIT_TARGET_ENEMY).  This is what Charge (100) and Intercept
--    (20252) both use.
--
-- 2. Effect2 is blanked.  It was SPELL_AURA_ADD_CASTER_HIT_TRIGGER at 100% --
--    "the next melee or ranged attack against this unit hits the warrior
--    instead".  Applied to an enemy that is not merely useless, it is
--    backwards: it would redirect the target's incoming attacks.
--
-- 3. AttributesEx5 loses 0x800 SPELL_ATTR5_IMPLIED_TARGETING ("auto-target
--    target of target", SharedDefines.h:566).  That is an ally-assist
--    convenience -- click your healer, hit their attacker.  Pointed at an
--    enemy it resolves to the enemy's target, which is usually the warrior
--    themselves.  Charge does not carry it.
--
--    AttributesEx6 swaps 0x4000000 for Charge's 0x800000
--    (SPELL_ATTR6_TAPS_IMMEDIATELY), so charging in tags the mob the way
--    Charge and Intercept do.
--
-- Deliberately NOT copied from Charge:
--
--   SPELL_ATTR1_NO_THREAT (0x400).  Charge generates no threat and does not
--   engage.  For a tank's opener that is exactly wrong -- Intervene keeps
--   normal threat so the charge actually pulls.
--
--   SPELL_ATTR0_NOT_IN_COMBAT_ONLY_PEACEFUL.  Neither spell has it any more
--   (woa_2026_08_08_05.sql stripped it from Charge), but Charge has the
--   restriction re-imposed in C++ by spell_warr_charge_in_combat unless the
--   warrior has Juggernaut.  That script is registered on -100 only, so
--   Intervene is freely usable in combat -- which is the whole point of giving
--   Protection its own version.
--
-- The -10% damage debuff survives the redesign and reads better than it did:
-- on an ally it was a threat-management tax, on an enemy it is straightforward
-- mitigation for the target you just committed to.  200640 is renamed from
-- "Interceded" to "Staggered" and re-pointed at the enemy.
--
-- Core's spell_warr_intervene (src/server/scripts/Spells/spell_warrior.cpp:128)
-- is unregistered.  It hooks EFFECT_1 / SPELL_EFFECT_APPLY_AURA to cast 59667,
-- the threat reduction on the intervened ally.  With Effect2 blanked the hook
-- can never fire, but leaving the registration in place would imply the ability
-- still has an ally half.
--
-- Rage: still free and still generates none.  Charge's +10 rage is masked to
-- Charge alone, and Improved Charge is an Arms talent.
--
-- Spells:
--   3411   = Intervene
--   200640 = Staggered (was Interceded)
--   100    = Charge, 20252 = Intercept -- the two spells this now mirrors
-- ============================================================

-- ------------------------------------------------------------
-- Retire core's ally-side script
-- ------------------------------------------------------------
DELETE FROM `spell_script_names` WHERE `ScriptName` = 'spell_warr_intervene';

